{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the advantage.</b> When he finished commanding regarding fear of Elohim, he returned to instruct him in worldly matters — which trade is good that he may live from it and there be no sin in it. He said: for the advantage of working the land is in everything — even the king, who has none above him, is served by the field on account of his need, for from it is his sustenance."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:42.543324418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}